# Spec §4.2 and §5.3. Derived status of a recurring task in calendar mode.
# Dates and times in the device's local time; the day starts at 00:00.
# "today" is the local date of "now".
# P = the greatest ocurrenciaCubierta among its completions; if never completed,
# P = the day before creadaEn. N = the first occurrence after P.
#   today < N: waiting; today = N: pending; today > N: overdue (only once).
# Waiting progress = (now − waiting start) / (start of N − waiting start),
# with waiting start = the most recent completadoEn or, if there is none, creadaEn.
# It is a fraction between 0 and 1, compared exactly.
# A day of the month that does not exist in a month (e.g. 31 in June) falls on the last
# day of that month.
# "the task has a completion ... that covers ..." are already stored
# completions (for example, synced from another device), with their
# ocurrenciaCubierta as is. When the step does not give the time of the completion,
# that time does not affect the result. With completions, creadaEn does not affect it.
Feature: Calendar recurring task status

  # Calendar recurring task status 1
  # Weekly never completed, before its first occurrence: waiting,
  # with progress since creadaEn.
  Scenario Outline: Calendar recurring task status 1
    Given a weekly recurring task on <days> created on <created>
    When I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>

    Examples:
      | days           | created             | now                 | progress |
      | martes, jueves | 2026-07-15T12:00:00 | 2026-07-15T18:00:00 | 0.5      |
      | domingo        | 2026-07-13T00:00:00 | 2026-07-16T00:00:00 | 0.5      |
      | lunes, viernes | 2026-07-18T00:00:00 | 2026-07-18T12:00:00 | 0.25     |
      | sábado         | 2026-07-13T08:00:00 | 2026-07-14T12:00:00 | 0.25     |

